    "body": "### Contact Details (e.g. Tox ID or email)\n\n_No response_\n\n### qTox Version\n\nv1.18.3\n\n### Commit Hash\n\nb7802b42dcf5f68474eb4d6db66c004e3ca50848\n\n### Toxcore Version\n\n0.2.20\n\n### Qt Version\n\n6.8.1\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Start qTox\n2. Send the message \"祝秘\" to someone\n\n### Observed Behavior\n\nThe displayed message becomes \"㊗️㊙️\"\n\n### Expected Behavior\n\nThis should not be emojified. For example if I write \"お祝いは秘密\" it becoming \"お㊗️いは㊙️密\" is weird.\n\n### Reproducibility\n\nAlways\n\n### Operating System\n\nOther (please specify)\n\n### Operating System version/distro/name/etc.\n\nTested on Windows 11 and Linux Mint 22.2\n\n### Relevant log output\n\n```shell\n\n```",
